sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-21> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Levin proposes that aging is due to the degradation of endogenous bioelectric pattern memories required throughout life to maintain tissue order, so that solutions to aging need to target this information scaffold as well as cell-level rejuvenation (e.g. Yamanaka factors).";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aging may result from degraded bioelectric pattern memories that maintain tissue order";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “Applications and a Roadmap Toward a Radical Regenerative Medicine › A Better Understanding of Disease: From Molecular Markers to Physiological Patterns”. Scope: Aging tissues in multicellular animals"
}
